WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:01.967
Seaside duels.

00:00:01.967 --> 00:00:03.195
Heartbroken mothers.

00:00:03.195 --> 00:00:04.447
Vengeful thugs.

00:00:04.548 --> 00:00:10.050
As 1923's first season comes to a close the
growing Dutton family sits more precariously

00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:11.050
than ever.

00:00:12.087 --> 00:00:16.580
If fans of Taylor Sheridan's work haven't
noticed by now, one of the prevailing themes

00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:18.490
is the importance of family.

00:00:18.490 --> 00:00:22.400
From his early features like Hell or High
Water to Sylvester Stallone's crime comedy

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:27.701
Tulsa King, Sheridan's stories have almost
all revolved around the power and pull of family.

00:00:27.701 --> 00:00:32.087
Nowhere is this truer than in Yellowstone
and its spin-off 1923.

00:00:32.087 --> 00:00:36.480
This theme runs most obviously through the
story of Jacob Dutton and his clan, and how

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:40.820
there is nothing more that motivates the staunch
patriarch than his love of his kin.

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:43.510
He does everything for them and them alone.

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:47.280
The finale makes clear that families come
in all manner of shapes and sizes, and it

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:51.370
doesn't matter what shape it may be — family
is all that matters.

00:00:51.370 --> 00:00:56.090
Tragically, injustice abounds in 1923 as much
as it does in the real world when the law

00:00:56.090 --> 00:01:00.910
comes to arrest rancher Zane Davis' wife for
the crime of marrying a white man.

00:01:00.910 --> 00:01:05.610
At the same time, Jacob's family is falling
apart, with his new niece miscarrying a pregnancy,

00:01:05.610 --> 00:01:09.480
and the family home on the verge of being
taken by Donald Whitfield.

00:01:09.865 --> 00:01:12.911
"The word decent doesn't apply to me."

00:01:12.911 --> 00:01:19.130
While freedom to live, work and love are generally
held as fundamental human rights, 1923 takes

00:01:19.130 --> 00:01:23.799
a hard look at the many ways these needs are
denied to large populations of people.

00:01:23.799 --> 00:01:28.960
By the end of Season 1, many of the characters
can see that freedom is not always guaranteed.

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:33.369
On the reservation, Teonna's fight for freedom
forces her to kill, pushing back against the

00:01:33.369 --> 00:01:38.064
oppression she faces after being taken from
her family and forced into a Catholic boarding school.

00:01:38.064 --> 00:01:42.329
In their attempt to take away her identity
through cruelty and torture, they inadvertently

00:01:42.329 --> 00:01:44.119
unleash her inner warrior.

00:01:44.119 --> 00:01:47.869
Now, if she wants to live free, she must fight
harder than ever before.

00:01:47.869 --> 00:01:52.341
Luckily, she stands alongside her rescuers,
her father, and Pete Plenty Clouds, as they

00:01:52.341 --> 00:01:56.280
look to start a new life together while on
the run from America's lawmen.

00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:58.990
The Duttons, meanwhile, face their own fight
for freedom.

00:01:58.990 --> 00:02:04.310
As a new day in America dawns and more and
more laws begin to strip them of their sovereignty,

00:02:04.310 --> 00:02:07.149
Jacob Dutton is forced to fight fire with
fire.

00:02:07.149 --> 00:02:11.290
That may mean a fight in the fields with guns
and guts, or it might mean a battle in the

00:02:11.290 --> 00:02:16.080
boardroom, facing off against ruthless businessmen
who would use guile and cunning to take from

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:17.950
him everything that he's built.

00:02:19.096 --> 00:02:24.750
Not long after the events of 1883, the Wild
West is already fading as pioneers begin building

00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:28.190
up the West and the law starts to make its
way to the frontier.

00:02:28.190 --> 00:02:32.860
By the era of 1923, however, the mountains
of Montana are firmly becoming part of the

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:33.860
modern world.

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:37.769
Though they are still well behind the big
cities like New York and San Francisco, we've

00:02:37.769 --> 00:02:42.000
seen through the course of the season that
automobiles are slowly taking over for horses,

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:45.569
and electricity is finally finding its way
into homes.

00:02:45.569 --> 00:02:50.069
Jacob Dutton has been resistant to such change,
though his wife Cara seems happy to have a

00:02:50.069 --> 00:02:52.820
washing machine to make her household chores
easier.

00:02:52.820 --> 00:02:57.110
In the finale, we see the truest extent of
modern changes, as horse hitches in the city

00:02:57.110 --> 00:03:01.740
have been removed from the street to make
way for automobile parking spaces, and new

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:06.000
20th century laws allow bankers and tycoons
to take away a person's house and home through

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:07.880
shady business deals.

00:03:07.880 --> 00:03:12.390
Jacob Dutton, a man born before the Civil
War, is a remnant of an old world where problems

00:03:12.390 --> 00:03:17.290
were solved with a fist or a gun, and, somewhat
paradoxically, neighbors respected each other's

00:03:17.290 --> 00:03:19.420
livelihoods and cared for their community.

00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:24.299
Likewise, Teonna's people, who once roamed
free and loved the land, now have modern American

00:03:24.299 --> 00:03:26.720
laws dictating their way of life.

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:31.332
Change is inevitable, and if 1923 tells us
anything, it's that while change can be good,

00:03:31.332 --> 00:03:34.672
it can also cause harm when controlled by
the wrong people.

00:03:34.773 --> 00:03:40.899
"I have compassion, but I have no mercy."

00:03:41.386 --> 00:03:45.360
While on the run from the law throughout the
later portion of Season 1, Teonna has been

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:49.620
forced to kill several of her pursuers before
she gets discovered by her father.

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:53.390
With a U.S. Marshal on their tail, they're
forced to flee to Wyoming where they hope

00:03:53.390 --> 00:03:57.780
to join a new clan of Comanche down south
and begin a new chapter of their lives.

00:03:57.780 --> 00:04:01.860
However, with so much turmoil in her young
life, Teonna defies her father and begins

00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:05.890
a romance with Pete Plenty Clouds, partially
due to the fact that her experiences this

00:04:05.890 --> 00:04:08.970
season have taught her that tomorrow isn't
guaranteed.

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:12.620
These lessons have also been learned by the
Duttons, who are ready to take matters into

00:04:12.620 --> 00:04:17.690
their own hands, rather than to wait out the
return of their intended savior, Spencer.

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:21.280
With Donald Whitfield at their door ready
to take the land beneath their feet and steal

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:26.350
the Yellowstone Ranch, and Banner Creighton
ready to see them all dead in a hail of gunfire,

00:04:26.350 --> 00:04:27.960
waiting is not an option.

00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:32.860
For all of our protagonists, prosperity and
survival depend on taking action immediately,

00:04:32.860 --> 00:04:34.970
because there may not be a later.

00:04:34.970 --> 00:04:38.490
This is a wisdom that Spencer and Alexandra
learn earlier this season.

00:04:38.490 --> 00:04:42.800
Like Teonna and Pete, they jump headfirst
into a romance because the dangers of life

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:44.820
allow no room for patience.

00:04:44.820 --> 00:04:49.090
They were right not to waste the time, as
they've been forced apart by fate by the end

00:04:49.090 --> 00:04:50.090
of the season.

00:04:51.216 --> 00:04:55.919
In the season finale, Spencer and Alexandra
finally set sail for American shores, but

00:04:55.919 --> 00:04:58.430
they are forced to deal with a new problem.

00:04:58.430 --> 00:05:02.300
This time, though, it's not the harsh sting
of nature that interferes with their love,

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:06.830
but the spite of a spurned lover — Alex's
former husband-in-waiting Arthur.

00:05:06.830 --> 00:05:10.830
In the finale, it's revealed that Arthur is
more than just Alex's ex-fiancé, but the

00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:15.000
Earl of Sussex, whose father is a prince in
the line of succession.

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:19.151
With all three forced together during their
voyage on the RMS Majestic ocean liner, Alex

00:05:19.151 --> 00:05:24.020
is initially determined to avoid a confrontation
by staying in her cabin for the entirety of

00:05:24.020 --> 00:05:25.020
their trip.

00:05:25.020 --> 00:05:29.090
But when frustrations with their situation
boil over, Alex and Spencer agree that the

00:05:29.090 --> 00:05:32.080
only way to deal with their problems is head
on.

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:36.300
Unfortunately, this leads to a new crisis,
as Arthur challenges Spencer to a duel on

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:37.419
the deck.

00:05:37.419 --> 00:05:41.169
Spencer wins the day but is forced to throw
Arthur overboard when the bitter ex-lover

00:05:41.169 --> 00:05:45.590
pulls a pistol, leading to the hunter's arrest
and expulsion from the ship and a possibly

00:05:45.590 --> 00:05:48.696
permanent separation from the woman he loves.

00:05:49.456 --> 00:05:54.870
More than any series yet, 1923 appears to
be Taylor Sheridan's way of making crystal

00:05:54.870 --> 00:05:57.330
clear how he feels about the rich and powerful.

00:05:57.330 --> 00:06:01.610
More than once he's shown the villainous mining
magnate Donald Whitfield using his wealth

00:06:01.610 --> 00:06:05.240
to attain control over others in perverse
and corrupt ways.

00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:09.850
In a revealing moment, Whitfield spells out
what might be the series' biggest message.

00:06:09.850 --> 00:06:13.960
Chatting with his crony Banner Creighton,
Whitfield says bluntly that true wealth isn't

00:06:13.960 --> 00:06:17.800
just being rich, it’s being so rich that
you can't possibly spend all of your money

00:06:17.800 --> 00:06:19.210
in your own lifetime.

00:06:19.615 --> 00:06:22.194
"I could never spend all the money I've made.

00:06:22.194 --> 00:06:27.580
What I do now ensures that my great grandchildren
can't either.

00:06:27.580 --> 00:06:31.540
To achieve this generational wealth, Whitfield
proclaims that he must take from those he

00:06:31.540 --> 00:06:34.830
deems unworthy, and his target is the Dutton
ranch.

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:38.830
In one of the episode's final scenes, he even
admits that he feels no need to act with honor

00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:39.830
or respect.

00:06:39.830 --> 00:06:45.211
Loud and clear, 1923 tells us that the search
for power and money leads to evil, and that

00:06:45.211 --> 00:06:49.556
wealth alone is not a signal of virtue, nobility,
or strength of character.

00:06:50.789 --> 00:06:55.660
By the conclusion of the first season of 1923,
Jacob Dutton has found himself in a world

00:06:55.660 --> 00:06:56.660
of trouble.

00:06:56.660 --> 00:07:01.000
He's been surrounded by his enemies: the rich
and powerful Donald Whitfield and the thuggish

00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:02.680
and vengeful Banner Creighton.

00:07:02.680 --> 00:07:07.250
While Jacob wants justice for the family members
who Banner directly and indirectly murdered,

00:07:07.250 --> 00:07:10.700
the law is making it more and more difficult
to get it.

00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:14.880
However, Jacob is far from blameless, as the
feud begins when he hangs Banner's men for

00:07:14.880 --> 00:07:18.040
trespassing on his land so his sheep could
graze.

00:07:18.040 --> 00:07:22.040
Jacob knows that the law isn't always about
justice, and as a man of the Old West, he

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:23.800
takes it into his own hands.

00:07:23.800 --> 00:07:27.970
This decision comes back to bite him, as the
case against Banner falls apart due to Dutton's

00:07:27.970 --> 00:07:30.530
hasty attempt at frontier justice.

00:07:30.530 --> 00:07:35.190
The law also isn't helping Teonna on the reservation,
as it's unwilling to consider the abuse and

00:07:35.190 --> 00:07:39.220
torture she receives at the hands of the sisters
at the Catholic boarding school.

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:43.210
Likewise, Spencer's story is also marred by
the corruption of law enforcement.

00:07:43.210 --> 00:07:47.530
Aboard the Majestic, Arthur's royal father
uses his position to shift the law in his

00:07:47.530 --> 00:07:52.560
favor by having Spencer removed from the ocean
liner and ripped from Alex's arms after Spencer

00:07:52.560 --> 00:07:53.780
defeats his son.

00:07:53.780 --> 00:07:59.550
"This ship sails under a British flag, and
a prince in succession has order you removed

00:07:59.550 --> 00:08:00.550
from the vessel."

00:08:01.084 --> 00:08:05.470
While many believe that the future is what
they make it to be, many others believe destiny

00:08:05.470 --> 00:08:10.349
to be preordained, even if we feel like we
can exercise free will in the moment.

00:08:10.349 --> 00:08:15.150
"Nothing Left to Lose" solidifies that 1923
clearly stands in the latter camp, with its

00:08:15.150 --> 00:08:19.340
characters under the impression destiny is
not something they have much of a say in.

00:08:19.340 --> 00:08:22.740
For Jack and Elizabeth, destiny has dire consequences.

00:08:22.740 --> 00:08:26.840
We learn that the attack on the ranch earlier
in the season may have permanently impaired

00:08:26.840 --> 00:08:29.080
Elizabeth's ability to bear children.

00:08:29.080 --> 00:08:33.320
Following her miscarriage, she ponders what
kind of life she will have if she is unable

00:08:33.320 --> 00:08:34.610
to start a family.

00:08:34.610 --> 00:08:38.580
In response, Jack declares that if it's not
their destiny to be parents, then they shall

00:08:38.580 --> 00:08:41.289
find out together what their destiny really
is.

00:08:41.289 --> 00:08:45.940
He doesn't feel that he chose Elizabeth for
his wife, but that destiny made the match

00:08:45.940 --> 00:08:47.779
and he went along for the ride.

00:08:47.779 --> 00:08:51.950
He also wonders if perhaps their destiny is
to raise someone else's children — orphans

00:08:51.950 --> 00:08:56.089
who need a home — just as his Aunt Cara
did when she and Jacob arrived in Montana

00:08:56.089 --> 00:09:00.087
after the death of James and Margaret Dutton
left their children alone.

00:09:00.926 --> 00:09:05.290
As Yellowstone has demonstrated for years,
a central theme in the Dutton shared universe

00:09:05.290 --> 00:09:07.100
is that of a found family.

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:10.980
In the parent series, we've seen this play
out more than once, with son Jamie discovered

00:09:10.980 --> 00:09:13.570
to have been adopted by John Dutton as a baby.

00:09:13.570 --> 00:09:18.420
Later, he brought a wayward Rip Wheeler into
the fold, if not as family, then as the next

00:09:18.420 --> 00:09:19.660
best thing.

00:09:19.660 --> 00:09:23.750
Dutton's daughter Beth, along with her husband
Rip, later fostered young Carter, an orphan

00:09:23.750 --> 00:09:28.100
without a home, proving that family is built
off of far more than blood.

00:09:28.100 --> 00:09:33.220
In 1923 we learn that it was Jacob and Cara
who raised James and Margaret's children as

00:09:33.220 --> 00:09:35.029
their own after their deaths.

00:09:35.029 --> 00:09:39.540
What's more, in the finale, we get our first
hints that this custom of caring for the unwanted

00:09:39.540 --> 00:09:43.720
and orphaned may be something of a family
custom that took roots decades before the

00:09:43.720 --> 00:09:45.220
events of Yellowstone.

00:09:45.220 --> 00:09:49.540
Following Elizabeth's miscarriage, Jack Dutton
suggests that rather than have their own children,

00:09:49.540 --> 00:09:53.220
their future may see them adopting children
who need a home as a way of expanding their

00:09:53.220 --> 00:09:56.130
family and continuing the Dutton legacy.

00:09:56.130 --> 00:10:00.490
Could this mean that Kevin Costner's John
Dutton is the child of an adopted Dutton himself?

00:10:00.490 --> 00:10:04.230
This would certainly establish a thematic
link between the two series and explain John's

00:10:04.230 --> 00:10:06.680
penchant for caring for lost souls.

00:10:06.680 --> 00:10:10.420
For now, however, that's a question best left
for another time.

00:10:11.166 --> 00:10:15.790
As the Beatles so fondly reminded listeners
in their hit "All You Need Is Love," love

00:10:15.790 --> 00:10:18.519
is a powerful and unpredictable force.

00:10:18.519 --> 00:10:23.600
Throughout Season 1 of 1923, every hero has
to put their faith in this joyous feeling.

00:10:23.600 --> 00:10:27.930
Jacob has mentioned repeatedly how his love
for his wife Cara has kept him strong, while

00:10:27.930 --> 00:10:31.750
Jack's love for his wife Elizabeth has seen
him through the death of his father.

00:10:31.750 --> 00:10:37.115
Even Teonna is finding solace in her newfound
love as she escapes a life of torment and anguish.

00:10:37.115 --> 00:10:41.450
However, the lesson may have been learned
best by Spencer Dutton, the prodigal son of

00:10:41.450 --> 00:10:45.579
the Yellowstone ranch who begins the series
estranged from the family and seeking his

00:10:45.579 --> 00:10:47.570
fortune a world away.

00:10:47.570 --> 00:10:51.240
Spencer never felt like he ever needed anybody
but himself, but when an adventure-seeking

00:10:51.240 --> 00:10:55.860
maiden named Alexandra hitches her ride to
his, he discovers the power of love and all

00:10:55.860 --> 00:10:57.770
it could help him accomplish.

00:10:57.770 --> 00:11:01.910
But he also has to deal with the dark side,
and the pain love can cause when it is taken

00:11:01.910 --> 00:11:03.260
away from you.

00:11:03.260 --> 00:11:07.440
Separated from Alex at the close of the finale,
Spencer's desperate cries to his new wife

00:11:07.440 --> 00:11:11.842
prove that no matter what anyone takes from
you, love binds forever.

